<title>USA: Siemens unit, Wisc. Int. in Subic Bay deal.</title>
<headline>Siemens unit, Wisc. Int. in Subic Bay deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siemens Power Generation and Wisconsin International Electric Power Ltd said on Monday they signed a memo of understanding to build a $75 million power plant at Subic Bay in the Philippines.</p>
<p>The 150-MG, natural gas turbine plant will be developed by Wisconsin, with Siemens as the turnkey contractor, for the Subic Bay Metropolitan Authority.</p>
<p>The plant will supply power to businesses locating in the former U.S. Navy base, now a free-trade zone.</p>
<p>Siemens Power is a unit of Siemens AG.</p>
</text>
